---
import Icon from "../ui/Icon.astro";
import Link from "../ui/Link.astro";
import Split from "./Split.astro";
---

<Split id="og-faq-title" eyebrow="FAQ" title="Questions, answered.">
  <p>Common questions about hosting OpenGeocode, what it costs, and how accurate it is.</p>
  <Link variant="standalone" href="/docs/">Read the documentation</Link>
  <div class="og-faq" slot="aside">
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>How do I use OpenGeocode?</summary>
      <p>
        Build a Pack with <code>og build</code>, then <code>og serve</code> it. See the <Link href="/docs/quickstart/">quickstart</Link>.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>What hardware do I need to host it?</summary>
      <p>
        Very little. This page's search serves the whole planet, a 27.7&nbsp;GB Pack, on 2 CPU cores with about
        0.2&nbsp;GB of memory of its own. The operating system's page cache holds the parts of the Pack that get used.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>How much does OpenGeocode cost?</summary>
      <p>Nothing. No API key, quota or per-lookup fee; you only pay for your machine.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>Does it work offline?</summary>
      <p>Yes. It only needs a connection to download data when building a Pack.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>Can I geocode a whole CSV?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes, with <code>open-geocode geocode batch</code>. See <Link href="/docs/guides/batch-csv/">batch geocoding</Link>.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>How accurate is it?</summary>
      <p>
        It leads the open-source geocoders on the MESSY STREETS benchmark. See the <Link href="/docs/benchmarks/">benchmarks</Link>.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>What about data and privacy?</summary>
      <p>It runs on your hardware, so no address leaves your network.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="og-faq-mark"><Icon name="x" size="sm" /></span>Is OpenGeocode open source?</summary>
      <p>Yes, MIT-licensed, on <Link href="https://github.com/open-geocode-rs/open-geocode">GitHub</Link>.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Split>

<style>
  /* Each question opens in place, its plus turning to a cross. */
  .og-faq {
    interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
  }

  .og-faq details + details {
    border-block-start: var(--border) solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .og-faq summary {
    align-items: flex-start;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    font: var(--type-ui-strong);
    gap: var(--space-3);
    list-style: none;
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
  }

  .og-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .og-faq summary:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--border-strong) solid var(--color-focus);
    outline-offset: calc(var(--space-0-5) * -1);
  }

  /* The cross turned an eighth reads as a plus. */
  .og-faq-mark {
    align-items: center;
    block-size: 1lh;
    color: var(--color-foreground-muted);
    display: inline-flex;
    flex: none;
    rotate: 45deg;
  }

  .og-faq [open] .og-faq-mark {
    rotate: 0deg;
  }

  .og-faq details p {
    color: var(--color-foreground-secondary);
    font: var(--type-ui);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 var(--space-6) var(--space-5) var(--space-12);
  }

  .og-faq code {
    font: var(--type-code-inline);
  }

  /* Opens and closes by height where the browser can animate it, and snaps elsewhere. */
  .og-faq details::details-content {
    block-size: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .og-faq details[open]::details-content {
    block-size: auto;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .og-faq-mark {
      transition: rotate var(--duration-enter) var(--ease-in-out);
    }

    .og-faq details::details-content {
      transition:
        block-size var(--duration-enter) var(--ease-out),
        content-visibility var(--duration-enter) allow-discrete;
    }
  }
</style>
